# Native SSH connection form (task 014 P4) with the on-screen keyboard forced (APPLAUNCH_OSK=force). The harness'
# config service answers the profile's defaults (192.168.1.1, 22, pi). Labels sit beside their fields. Shots: Host
# edits at once (keyboard up: no Connect / Help row, no status line) with a new host typed, Port on the number pad,
# User typed, the whole form after Esc (keyboard down: it fits under the header), the validation error of an empty
# host (Enter on User connects: the keyboard goes, "Host is required" in red on the status line), the keyboard back
# up on Host with the error under the field, the help page (F1) and back. The terminal is not shot.
# Review only: no golden; headers checked against the home grid's (run.sh header).
title ssh native form
review
env APPLAUNCH_OSK force
apps Settings Store CLI SSH Calculator
clock 20:30
wifi 70
bt on
home
header home ZERO
launch SSH
wait 300
key BACKSPACE
key BACKSPACE
key BACKSPACE
key BACKSPACE
key BACKSPACE
key BACKSPACE
key BACKSPACE
key BACKSPACE
key BACKSPACE
key BACKSPACE
key BACKSPACE
type 10.0.0.5
shot ssh_kb_host
header ssh_kb_host SSH
# Down: Port on the number pad (digits only), "22" replaced
key DOWN
key BACKSPACE
key BACKSPACE
type 2222
shot ssh_kb_port
# Down: User, "pi" replaced
key DOWN
key BACKSPACE
key BACKSPACE
type admin
shot ssh_kb_user
# Esc stops editing: the keyboard goes, the whole form shows (fields, Connect / Help, status line)
key ESC
wait 300
shot ssh_form
header ssh_form SSH
# Host emptied, Enter through Port and User connects: validation refuses, the keyboard goes
tapfield Host
key BACKSPACE
key BACKSPACE
key BACKSPACE
key BACKSPACE
key BACKSPACE
key BACKSPACE
key BACKSPACE
key BACKSPACE
key ENTER
key ENTER
key ENTER
wait 300
shot ssh_error
# a tap on Host: the keyboard is back, the error stays under the field
tapfield Host
wait 300
shot ssh_error_kb
# Esc, then F1: the help page (Esc / Left back to the form)
key ESC
key F1
wait 300
shot ssh_help
header ssh_help "SSH > Help" Help
key ESC
wait 300
shot ssh_help_back
